@@ -2,16 +2,21 @@
 import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
 ---
 <LegalLayout title="Privacy Policy">
-    <h2>1. An overview of data protection</h2>
-    <p><strong>General information</strong></p>
-    <p>The following information will provide you with an easy to navigate overview of what will happen with your personal data when you visit our website. The term “personal data” comprises all data that can be used to personally identify you. For detailed information about the subject matter of data protection, please consult our Data Protection Declaration, which we have included beneath this copy.</p>
-    
-    <h2>2. General information and mandatory information</h2>
-    <p><strong>Data protection</strong></p>
-    <p>The operators of this website and its pages take the protection of your personal data very seriously. Hence, we handle your personal data as confidential information and in compliance with the statutory data protection regulations and this Data Protection Declaration.</p>
-    <p>Whenever you use this website, a variety of personal information will be collected. Personal data comprises data that can be used to personally identify you. This Data Protection Declaration explains which data we collect as well as the purposes we use this data for. It also explains how, and for which purpose the information is collected.</p>
-    
-    <h2>3. Recording of data on our website</h2>
-    <p><strong>Cookies</strong></p>
-    <p>In some instances, our website and its pages use so-called cookies. Cookies do not cause any damage to your computer and do not contain viruses. The purpose of cookies is to make our website more user friendly, effective and more secure. Cookies are small text files that are placed on your computer and stored by your browser.</p>
+    <h2>Reading without an account</h2>
+    <p>You can read The DevTools Times without signing up. Our shared page layout does not load third-party analytics or advertising scripts. Fonts are hosted on this site, so loading a font does not contact a font provider.</p>
+
+    <h2>Account information</h2>
+    <p>Signing up and signing in require only a username and password. A nickname is enough: we do not ask for a real name, email address, phone number, or date of birth. The username identifies your account; the password is used to create or verify access to it.</p>
+    <p>Only when you submit an account form, your browser sends the username and password over HTTPS to our external account service at <code>us-central1-web-devrel-apps.cloudfunctions.net/times_cdn/api/</code> (the <code>register</code> or <code>login</code> endpoint). That service also receives connection information such as your IP address. The request omits cookies and the referring page URL.</p>
+    <p>These forms do not write credentials or authentication tokens to local storage, session storage, or cookies, and do not send form contents to analytics. The password field is cleared after each completed request. Your browser's password manager may offer to save credentials under your control.</p>
+    <p>This sample application does not expose the account service's retention settings or account export and deletion controls. We cannot confirm how long that service retains account data. Use a unique password and avoid personal information in your username.</p>
+
+    <h2>Reading lists and cookies</h2>
+    <p>When you change your reading list, the site saves article identifiers in a server-side session. A session cookie associates your browser with that list. We do not initialize an empty reading list merely because you visit a page. You can remove saved articles in the reading-list menu. Clearing site cookies disconnects this browser from the list; it does not itself delete server-side data.</p>
+
+    <h2>Other network requests</h2>
